v6 — Full Fix

Below are the complete, hardened files. Every P0 and P1 from the v5 audit is closed except for one documented residual (full namespace isolation — see the note at the end). The architecture is unchanged; the changes are:

· P0-B: subprocess.Popen(..., user=65534, group=65534, extra_groups=[]) on every tmux/xterm fork, cap_drop: [ALL] + no-new-privileges in compose, entrypoint unsets legacy secret env vars.
· P0-D: _assert_display_ownership(disp, user_id) gates send_keystrokes, resync, WS stream, and close. SSE payload is filtered per subscriber.
· P0-E: sendBeacon fires synchronously on pagehide; grace period moved server-side (revival check via last_touched).
· P1 auth fallback: startup fails closed if V2E_REQUIRE_AUTH=1 and no auth pubkey; publisher_id mismatch → 403 (not silent free-tier).
· P1 global state: UserWorkspace (per-user fork display, speaker state, command history, tmux socket); _ensure_user_fork() spawns :11xx displays lazily. speaker_playing is now local-per-user (no SSE broadcast).
· P1 _tls race: threading.local() at module scope.
· P2 nits: _ocr_pool separate from _capture_pool; WS ticket exchange (/api/ws-ticket, one-use 60s); kill xterm before tmux-server; can_popout refreshed via SSE.

